add(2,'A low pulse maintains the beat while a higher line repeatedly accents halfway between beats. Which rhythmic device is most prominent?', 'syncopation','augmentation','ritardando','hemiola','The higher line emphasizes offbeat eighth-note positions against a steady beat, producing syncopation. There is no progressive slowing, systematic doubling of a motive, or shift from two groups of three to three groups of two.',render('syncopation',events),evidence={'kind':'offbeat','pulseSeconds':.5,'offsetSeconds':.25})
add(2,'The same pitch pattern is played twice. Which change best describes the second presentation?', 'from connected to detached articulation','from soft to loud dynamics','from slow to fast tempo','from duple to triple grouping','The second version shortens sounding duration while retaining the same pitch onsets, tempo, and amplitude. That changes connected notes to detached notes; it does not change the meter, tempo, or dynamic level.',render('articulation',[dict(start=.3+i*.5,duration=.49,notes=[m]) for i,m in enumerate([60,62,64,65])]+[dict(start=3+i*.5,duration=.14,notes=[m]) for i,m in enumerate([60,62,64,65])]),evidence={'kind':'articulation','durations':[.49,.14],'onsetSpacing':.5})
add(2,'Which expressive change occurs across the repeated notes?', 'crescendo','diminuendo','accelerando','ritardando','Amplitude increases steadily while onset spacing and note duration remain constant. This is a crescendo, not a diminuendo or a tempo change.',render('crescendo',[dict(start=.3+i*.48,duration=.32,notes=[64],amp=.13+i*.065) for i in range(10)]),evidence={'kind':'dynamics','amplitudes':[.13+i*.065 for i in range(10)],'onsetSpacing':.48})
add(3,'TEXT SUBSTITUTE — A listening log describes a recurring orchestral refrain alternating with solo episodes, a continuo part, and sequential passages. Which work type best fits these clues?', 'Baroque solo concerto','Classical string quartet','Romantic character piece','Renaissance motet','Recurring orchestral ritornellos and solo episodes supported by continuo are characteristic of a Baroque solo concerto. A quartet lacks this orchestral/solo contrast, a character piece is commonly short solo music, and a motet is vocal. This tests descriptions, not recognition by ear.',proxy=True)
add(3,'TEXT SUBSTITUTE — An excerpt is described as a small jazz combo with rapid, angular single-note improvisation and frequent extended-chord substitutions. Which style is most consistent?', 'bebop','early New Orleans collective improvisation','ragtime piano','big-band swing arrangement','Virtuosic angular solo lines and complex harmonic substitutions in a small combo are characteristic bebop clues. New Orleans often emphasizes collective improvisation, ragtime is a composed piano tradition, and big-band swing uses larger arranged sections. No actual style-recognition audio is assessed here.',proxy=True)
add(3,'TEXT SUBSTITUTE — A performance description mentions a melodic improvisation within a raga, a sustained drone, and a recurring tala cycle. Which tradition is most consistent?', 'Indian classical music','Irish traditional reel playing','Argentine tango','Javanese gamelan','Raga, drone, and tala point to Indian classical traditions. The other traditions have their own melodic/rhythmic practices and are not defined by this combination. Descriptive knowledge cannot establish that you can identify this tradition by ear.',proxy=True)
